UnitMetaquoter::QuoteAddLiquidityV2
├── when the pool is not a registered target
│   └── it reverts with IP
└── given the pool is a registered target
    ├── when the target factory is not approved
    │   └── it reverts with AF
    └── given the target factory is approved
        ├── when the pool type is not a V2 type
        │   └── it reverts with PT
        ├── given the total supply is zero
        │   ├── when the geometric mean underflows the minimum liquidity
        │   │   └── it reverts with SafeMath: subtraction overflow
        │   ├── given the pool is stable
        │   │   ├── when the deposits are not equal
        │   │   │   └── it reverts with DE
        │   │   ├── when a donation makes the credited deposits unequal
        │   │   │   └── it reverts with DE
        │   │   ├── when the stable invariant is below the minimum
        │   │   │   └── it reverts with BK
        │   │   ├── when the deposits are equal
        │   │   │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and amount1Desired as amount1
        │   │   │   └── it returns liquidity as sqrt(amount0 * amount1) - MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY
        │   │   ├── when an offsetting desired deposit balances the credited deposits
        │   │   │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and amount1Desired as amount1
        │   │   │   └── it returns liquidity as sqrt(amount0 * amount1) - MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY
        │   │   ├── when donations are credited on both sides
        │   │   │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and amount1Desired as amount1
        │   │   │   └── it returns liquidity from the desired amounts, not the credited ones
        │   │   ├── when the deposits are equal at differing token decimals
        │   │   │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and amount1Desired as amount1
        │   │   │   └── it returns liquidity as sqrt(amount0 * amount1) - MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY
        │   │   ├── when the raw deposits match but the normalized ones do not
        │   │   │   └── it reverts with DE
        │   │   └── when the stable invariant equals the minimum
        │   │       └── it reverts with BK
        │   └── given the pool is not stable
        │       ├── when the first mint clears the minimum liquidity
        │       │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and amount1Desired as amount1
        │       │   └── it returns liquidity as sqrt(amount0 * amount1) - MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY
        │       └── when the minted liquidity is below the minimum
        │           └── it reverts with ILM
        └── given the total supply is nonzero
            ├── when amount0Desired is zero
            │   └── it reverts with IA
            ├── when reserve0 is zero
            │   └── it reverts with IL
            ├── when reserve1 is zero
            │   └── it reverts with IL
            └── given both reserves are nonzero
                ├── when the minted liquidity is zero
                │   └── it reverts with ILM
                ├── when a stable pool has drifted reserves
                │   ├── it trims amount1 to the drifted reserve ratio
                │   └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                ├── when the forward quotient does not fit uint256
                │   ├── it returns the full precision amount0Optimal as amount0 and amount1Desired as amount1
                │   └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                ├── when the high word is one below the denominator
                │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and the exact forward quote as amount1
                │   └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                ├── when the forward quotient is the first unrepresentable one
                │   ├── it returns the reverse quote as amount0 and amount1Desired as amount1
                │   └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                ├── when the forward quotient is exactly the uint256 max
                │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and the uint256 max as amount1
                │   └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                ├── when a non power of two product overflows
                │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and the exact forward quote as amount1
                │   └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                ├── given the optimal amount1 quote is at most amount1Desired
                │   ├── when the amounts are trimmed to amount1
                │   │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and amount1Optimal as amount1
                │   │   └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                │   ├── when the forward quote ties amount1Desired
                │   │   ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and the tying forward quote as amount1
                │   │   └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                │   └── when the forward product overflows and amount1 is trimmed
                │       ├── it returns amount0Desired as amount0 and the full precision amount1Optimal as amount1
                │       └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                └── given the optimal amount1 quote exceeds amount1Desired
                    ├── when amount1Desired is zero
                    │   └── it reverts with IA
                    ├── when the trimmed amount0 is quoted
                    │   ├── it returns amount0Optimal as amount0 and amount1Desired as amount1
                    │   └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
                    └── when the forward product overflows and amount0 is trimmed
                        ├── it returns the full precision amount0Optimal as amount0 and amount1Desired as amount1
                        └── it returns liquidity as the min of the reserve-proportional shares
